--- !u!114 &7906992478887642803
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 5280737227275109386}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b9787387f76b5354affff6655d1d0dd0, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  targetText: {fileID: 5079709197826889593}
  quotes:
  - '"Don''t come back home until you are a millionaire"\n\n-Mom'
  - '"Selling an organ here and there is probably fine"\n\n-Loan Shark'
  - '"I don''t understand it, but i''m proud of you"\n\n-Grandma'
  - '"It''s not losing, it''s investing"\n\n-Sketchy Guy'
  - "\"The odds are low\u2026 but never zero\"\\n\\n-Dad"
  - '"What is the worst that could happen?"\n\n-Shredding Machine Operator'
  - '"Imagine how much money you could win?"\n\n-Grandpa'
  - '"Gambling for 72 hours is good for you actually"\n\n-Some guy'
  - '"It ain''t a sin if you win"\n\n-Grandpa'
  - '"When life gives you lemons, bet''em all on black"\n\n-Unknown'
  - '"Poker? I hardly know her!"\n\n-Unknown'
  - '"There are worse things than financial ruin"\n\n-Dad'
  - '"Double or nothing"\n\n-Unknown'
  - '"Gamblers, gamblers, gamblers!!!"\n\n-Mr Booth'
  - '"God does not play Dice. I, however, do."\n\n-Mr Booth'
  - '"In hindsight red would have been a better choice"\n\n-Unknown'
  - '"Alea Iacta Est"\n\n-Julius Caesar'
  - '"All the world''s a casino, and all the men and women merely gamblers"\n\n-Shakespeare'
  - '"One bet a day keeps the repo man at bay"\n\n-Unknown'
  - "\"I always go all in\"\\n\\n-Olof H\xF6gberg "
  - '"Eat your betting money but don''t bet your eating money"\n\n-Duck Racing Proverb'
  - '"You can only lose %100 of your money, but you could win %999999"\n\n-Unknown '
  - '"I gambled many//chips on the roulette table//now autumn has come"\n\n-Traditional
    Haiku'
  - '"Risk it for the biscuit"\n\n-Cookie Monster'
  - '"The best throw of the dice is to throw them away."\n\n-Italian Proverb '
  - '"Which came first? Gambling or the gambler"\n\n-Unknown '
  - '"He''s all in"\n\n-Unknown'
  - '"All that clatters is not chips"\n\n-Shakespeare '
  - '"I bet, therefore I am"\n\n-Descartes'
  - "\"Quit while you're ahead. All the best gamblers do.\"\\n\\n-Baltasar Graci\xE1n
    y Morale"
  - '"Luck never gives, it only lends"\n\n-Swedish Proverb'
  - '"At the gambling table, there are no fathers and sons"\n\n-Chinese Proverb'
  - '"Behind bad luck comes Good Luck"\n\n-Unknown'
  - '"How much is your friendship worth?"\n\n-Loan Shark'
  - '"Go big and never go home!"\n\n-Mr. Booth'
  - '"Good luck or get f*cked"\n\n-Loan Shark'
  - '"In case of reckless gamblers, use the bat!"\n\n-Mr. Booth '
  - '"Use the items, they were hard to make."\n\n-Loan Shark'
  - '"Are you getting rich, son?"\n\n-Dad'
  - '"I used to be quite a card shark back in my days."\n\n-Loan Shark'
  - '"The casino always welcomes you!"\n\n-Mr. Booth'
  - '"Hurry, before they spot us."\n\n-Mr. Loan Shark'
  - '"Mmmmm, mmm mmmm mm"\n\n-Your friend who sold their mouth'
